IMPORT prelude

-- Part IVA of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Penalties, sections 38B to 38G.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- The value of a penalty unit is fixed by the Penalty Units Act 2009, which is not among the sources: amounts here are in penalty units.
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no, and NOTHING where it does not.

§ `Section 38B: offences and bodies corporate`

DECLARE `Kind of offender` IS ONE OF
    `an individual offender`
    `a body corporate offender`
    `some other offender`

-- A provision of an Act relating to offences is read as referring to bodies corporate as well as to individuals.
-- src:576 | A provision of an Act relating to offences shall be read as referring to bodies corporate as well as to individuals.
@ref s 38B (src:576)
GIVEN `the provision relates to offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      offender IS A `Kind of offender`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38B: the provision is read as referring to the offender` MEANS
    IF   `the provision relates to offences`
    THEN CONSIDER offender
         WHEN `some other offender` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 38C: penalties at the foot of sections and subsections`

-- A penalty, pecuniary or otherwise: a fine in penalty units and a term of imprisonment in months, either of which may be absent.
DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `fine in penalty units`       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `imprisonment in months`      IS A MAYBE NUMBER

DECLARE `Division of an Act` IS ONE OF
    `a section of the Act`
    `a subsection of the Act`

-- The penalty set out at the foot of a section or subsection indicates that a contravention of the section or subsection respectively is an offence against the Act
-- punishable on a finding of guilt by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.
-- src:578 | (1) The penalty, pecuniary or otherwise, set out:
-- src:579 | (a) at the foot of a section; or
-- src:580 | (b) at the foot of a subsection,
-- src:581 | of an Act indicates that a contravention of the section or of the subsection respectively, is an offence against the Act punishable on a finding of guilt by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.
@ref s 38C(1) (src:578-581)
GIVEN `the penalty is set out at the foot of` IS A `Division of an Act`
      `the contravention is of` IS A `Division of an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38C(1): the contravention is an offence against the Act` MEANS
    IF   `the penalty is set out at the foot of` EQUALS `the contravention is of`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 38C(1) (src:578-581)
GIVEN imposed IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `set out` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38C(1): a part of the penalty imposed does not exceed the same part of the penalty set out` MEANS
    CONSIDER imposed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        CONSIDER `set out`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST limit THEN amount AT MOST limit

@ref s 38C(1) (src:578-581)
GIVEN `the penalty set out` IS A Penalty
      `the penalty imposed` IS A Penalty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38C(1): the penalty imposed does not exceed the penalty set out` MEANS
    `s 38C(1): a part of the penalty imposed does not exceed the same part of the penalty set out` (`the penalty imposed`'s `fine in penalty units`) (`the penalty set out`'s `fine in penalty units`)
    AND `s 38C(1): a part of the penalty imposed does not exceed the same part of the penalty set out` (`the penalty imposed`'s `imprisonment in months`) (`the penalty set out`'s `imprisonment in months`)

-- Subsection (1) applies regardless of whether the penalty is expressed as a maximum penalty.
-- src:582 | (1AA) Subsection (1) applies regardless of whether the penalty is expressed as a maximum penalty.
@ref s 38C(1AA) (src:582)
GIVEN `the penalty is expressed as a maximum penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38C(1AA): subsection (1) applies to the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the penalty is expressed as a maximum penalty`
    WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE

-- A penalty is taken to be at the foot of a section or subsection even if an example or note appears after the penalty.
-- src:583 | (1A) For subsection (1), a penalty is taken to be at the foot of a section or subsection even if an example or note appears after the penalty.
@ref s 38C(1A) (src:583)
GIVEN `nothing other than an example or note appears after the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38C(1A): the penalty is taken to be at the foot of the section or subsection` MEANS
    IF `nothing other than an example or note appears after the penalty` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- A penalty expressed to apply only to a part of the section or subsection applies according to the tenor of the provision.
-- src:584 | (2) A penalty set out as provided in subsection (1) which is expressed to apply only to a part of the section or subsection applies according to the tenor of the provision.
@ref s 38C(2) (src:584)
GIVEN `the penalty is expressed to apply only to a part of the section or subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38C(2): the penalty applies according to the tenor of the provision` MEANS
    IF `the penalty is expressed to apply only to a part of the section or subsection` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Thing that section 38C treats as a section` IS ONE OF
    `a section of an Act`
    `a rule`
    `a regulation`
    `a by-law`
    `something other than a section, rule, regulation or by-law`

-- In this section, section includes a rule, regulation or by-law, and subsection has a corresponding meaning.
-- src:585 | (3) In this section section includes a rule, regulation or by-law and subsection has a corresponding meaning.
@ref s 38C(3) (src:585)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that section 38C treats as a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38C(3): the thing is a section for the purposes of section 38C` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `something other than a section, rule, regulation or by-law` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 38DC and 38F: fines under subordinate legislation`

-- The section applies to a provision of an Act authorising a maximum fine for an offence that may be imposed under subordinate legislation,
-- only if the provision does not expressly authorise a different maximum fine for a body corporate.
-- src:587 | (1) This section applies to a provision of an Act authorising a maximum fine for an offence that may be imposed under subordinate legislation under the Act only if the provision does not expressly authorise a maximum fine for a body corporate different from the maximum fine for an individual.
@ref s 38DC(1) (src:587)
GIVEN `the provision authorises a maximum fine for an offence that may be imposed under subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision expressly authorises a maximum fine for a body corporate different from the maximum fine for an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38DC(1): section 38DC applies to the provision` MEANS
    JUST (`the provision authorises a maximum fine for an offence that may be imposed under subordinate legislation`
          AND (NOT `the provision expressly authorises a maximum fine for a body corporate different from the maximum fine for an individual`))

-- The maximum fine is taken only to be the maximum fine for an individual.
-- src:588 | (2) The maximum fine is taken only to be the maximum fine for an individual that may be imposed under the subordinate legislation.
@ref s 38DC(2) (src:588)
GIVEN `section 38DC applies to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum fine for an individual authorised by the provision, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 38DC(2): the maximum fine for an individual that may be imposed under the subordinate legislation` MEANS
    IF `section 38DC applies to the provision` THEN JUST `the maximum fine for an individual authorised by the provision, in penalty units` ELSE NOTHING

-- The maximum fine for a body corporate is taken to be 5 times the maximum fine for an individual.
-- src:589 | (3) The maximum fine for a body corporate that may be imposed under the subordinate legislation is taken to be 5 times the maximum fine for an individual.
@ref s 38DC(3) (src:589)
GIVEN `section 38DC applies to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum fine for an individual authorised by the provision, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 38DC(3): the maximum fine for a body corporate that may be imposed under the subordinate legislation` MEANS
    IF `section 38DC applies to the provision` THEN JUST (5 TIMES `the maximum fine for an individual authorised by the provision, in penalty units`) ELSE NOTHING

-- Subordinate legislation may prescribe a fine for an offence against the legislation.
-- src:591 | (1) Subordinate legislation may prescribe a fine for an offence against the legislation.
@ref s 38F(1) (src:591)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence against the subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38F(1): the subordinate legislation may prescribe a fine for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence against the subordinate legislation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- The fine prescribed must not exceed 100 penalty units.  The section has effect subject to the Act under which the legislation is made.
-- Note for subsection (2): because of section 38DC, the maximum fine for a body corporate is 500 penalty units.
-- src:592 | (2) The fine prescribed must not exceed 100 penalty units.
-- src:593 | Note for subsection (2)
-- src:594 | Because of section 38DC, the maximum fine for a body corporate that may be imposed under the subordinate legislation is 500 penalty units.
-- src:595 | (3) This section has effect subject to the Act under which the legislation is made.
@ref s 38F(2), (3) (src:592-595)
GIVEN `the fine prescribed, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
      `the Act under which the legislation is made provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38F(2): the fine prescribed is within the limit` MEANS
    IF   `the Act under which the legislation is made provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the fine prescribed, in penalty units` AT MOST 100)

§ `Section 38G: civil penalties`

-- A reference to a civil penalty being imposed or required to be paid for a contravention indicates that the contravention may result in a penalty not exceeding the penalty specified in, or prescribed for the purposes of, the provision.
-- src:597 | In an Act, a reference to a civil penalty (however described) being imposed or required to be paid for a contravention of a provision of the Act indicates that the contravention may lead to a penalty being imposed not exceeding the penalty specified in, or prescribed for the purposes of, the provision.
@ref s 38G (src:597)
GIVEN `the civil penalty specified or prescribed, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
      `the civil penalty imposed or required to be paid, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38G: the civil penalty is within the penalty specified or prescribed` MEANS
    JUST (`the civil penalty imposed or required to be paid, in penalty units` AT MOST `the civil penalty specified or prescribed, in penalty units`)
